hen meaning that  in the eyes of other children  he was likely a prime candidate for  bullying that's just the way kids are  like if you're different in a negative  way  they will most likely try and pick on  you in some way  perhaps he suffered abuse in a similar  way to deku although instead of going  home to a loving mother like income  midoriya  all might had no one to support him and  also no one to look up to  anyway i had a list of four additional  things that should be touched on if they  decide to do a prequel series  and let me know if i've missed anything  that you would like to see if this does  happen  to start with i think it would be a  great opportunity for us to learn about  the history of ua  for example who founded it and how it  rose to be the most respected hero  school in japan  the creation of ue would obviously be  before all might's time you know he's  not that old  but i think it's something that could  still be touched upon in any prequel  series  as pure speculation i would imagine that  ua was founded by a  former vigilante as we know that before  licensed pro heroes became a thing  random vigilantes would just suit up in  costumes and pretend to be heroes  this makes them the most experienced  when it comes to actually teaching kids  how to be pros furthermore we'd get to  see the other types of heroes that  attended ua at the same time as the  symbol of peace  you know perhaps maybe some that we have  encountered during our time in the  series  personally i would imagine that this  samurai hero who ranked number nine on  the charts  he's quite old so maybe he was even a  t-shirt at ua when all might was there  in the same way that gran torino was i  reckon they're roughly the same age  but yeah i think it would also be good  just to see all my's classmates and you  know where they are now are they  heroes in japan still or are they across  the world this would be a really  interesting thing to touch on  secondly a prequel is a great chance to  show off new and original quirks  possessed by all for one that we've  never seen before in the words of gran  torino  afo's abilities in kamino were  completely different from when they  faced him  six years earlier so could you imagine  how much more different they would be  during all might's young years when he  was in high school overhaul said that  all for one stole quirks to gain power  and a really effective way of doing that  is stealing the quirks of established  professional heroes  not only would the quirks themselves be  really great but obviously other heroes  would be afraid to  oppose all for one for fear of losing  their own powers  so yeah we would definitely need more  focus on all for one  because i mean when we look at the main  series being real  it's a story about deku and shigaraki  all my and afo were well past their  prime  you know as soon as we met them really  so it would be good to have a series  where we see  afo at his top and all might on his way  to the top  thirdly i want to know about any great  heroes during this era that maybe all  might  took inspiration from even if only a  little bit it goes without saying that  nana shimura and gran torino had  profound  impacts on him but what about the hero  known as brave  back in the cultural festival gentle  criminal mentioned how all might  crimson riot and brave were heroes that  left their shining mark on history  however unlike the rest brave is a  totally unknown entity we have no idea  what he or she might look like  but perhaps brave could have more  prominence in the prequel series  whether they be a retired hero or an  ex-vigilante  there's also actually a hero called mr  brave in the main story  who can shapeshift his hair into various  tools so perhaps he was inspired by the  real brave  in much the same way that red riot was  inspired by crimson riot  and deku is inspired by allmight but  yeah the point is  a new prequel series could offer more  insight into iconic japanese heroes that  maybe we just don't have time to learn  about in the main series  finally any almighty prequel would have  to show us how he motivated and changed  the part  of other people around him this is  something that deku has achieved  numerous times with the likes of  todoroki kota tenure bakugou ochako  and probably some other people that i  didn't mention in one way or another  each of the characters i mentioned  have either aspired to be better or have  had their view of the world changed  directly  because of deku's presence similarly a  young almighty would definitely have an  effect on the people around him  with his natural charisma his charm and  just his talent  so knight i said that both deku and all  might have the same fire and drive  inside them  so i'd love to see how all might went  around like winning the hearts and minds  of people  even as a young kid if this news about  touhou creating a new series is legit  then i i imagine how many series it  would be because  if it was only one season and it was  this all my prequel idea  then i think it should span from all my  younger days to his ua days  and then include the death of  nanashimura and flash forward to his  fight with all for one  that occurred six years before the main  series that would wrap up the timeline  very nicely and give us  pretty much everything we need to know  going into my here academia  also it's just nice to sometimes watch  things in chronological order  like star wars i guess you could say  regardless of whether it happens or not  i feel like all my time in america will  100 become its own movie one day  and i i have a few reasons for thinking  this but they're partially based on  comments from hirokoshi  that he wasn't really sure of a way to  top heroes rising because you know in  the first movie he had  all might and deku working together then  the second movie he has bakugo and deku  working together  so it's like what do you do for the next  one and in my opinion it'd just be good  to change  almost change the cast completely but  still have it with characters that we're  familiar with  so in all my prequel if they're gonna do  more movies i think it will have to come  eventually  anyway those are my thoughts on what i'd  like to see from an almighty prequel  and i hope this licensed global thing is  what we think it is  because i'd love to see any spin-off  series to be honest but you know you  know my preferred option but i would  love to see any spin-off  let me know what you guys think down  below would you rather have a vigilante  spin-off or an almighty spin-off or  something else  remember to subscribe if you want more  videos like this and until the next one  peace out  you
 

